    "poster_id": 363884,
    "post_rendered": "Two circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/6/2e6b05233b78f73b4a5136e81e24b14166ce05d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega , \\Omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"16\" > intersect in distinct points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f642cbbd390b4882363ab6b5c2906dbf6be6cc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" > a line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/6/2e6b05233b78f73b4a5136e81e24b14166ce05d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega , \\Omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"16\" > in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/652d9e9762895d2a55d683c43f4f3ab21c35184d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C,D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" > respectively such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > lies between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/652d9e9762895d2a55d683c43f4f3ab21c35184d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C,D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" > another line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/6/2e6b05233b78f73b4a5136e81e24b14166ce05d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega , \\Omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"16\" > in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/0/250f765e0f0b3842f9d095dc0a3569905d344ce8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E,F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" > respectively such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > lies between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/e/c9efd2c5b053e9918dda75c0c3d9571f825e5ca9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B,F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" > and <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/7/84781a18751b3ae65a77ced790d7916048378b75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE=CD$\"  width=\"82\" height=\"12\" >.</span> Furthermore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"12\" > intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/6/2e6b05233b78f73b4a5136e81e24b14166ce05d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega , \\Omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"16\" > in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d559f1ae366d6c7ddffa20b504ac135a430839.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P,Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" > respectively and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e929dc6c21edf7f11254db489376105e0abc1b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M,N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" > are midpoints of the arcs <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/0/7f076ed390652c6508f1d215377af1a857d3d9e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB,QB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" >.</span>  Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44d8ec0d36d71636fe127e5fef0e3eb656b3d07f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CNMF$\"  width=\"64\" height=\"12\" > is a cyclic quadrilateral.",
    "post_canonical": "Two circles $\\omega , \\Omega$ intersect in distinct points $A,B$ a line through $B$ intersects $\\omega , \\Omega$ in $C,D$ respectively such that $B$ lies between $C,D$ another line through $B$ intersects $\\omega , \\Omega$ in $E,F$ respectively such that $E$ lies between $B,F$ and $FE=CD$. Furthermore $CF$ intersects $\\omega , \\Omega$ in $P,Q$ respectively and $M,N$ are midpoints of the arcs $PB,QB$.  Prove that $CNMF$ is a cyclic quadrilateral.",
