   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 14682854,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 2060225,
    "poster_id": 363884,
    "post_rendered": "We call a function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/c/3ac781cb2cf4524183829aba8c612e3ff4801dd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f: \\mathbb{Q}^+ \\to \\mathbb{Q}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" > <i>good</i> if for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/c/98c51b80b0483c998fa70aca1553094b65978d49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y \\in \\mathbb{Q}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" > we have: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/0/e807cc7f102c1f57b61932ddf7971b6590ce655d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"$$f(x)+f(y)\\geq 4f(x+y).$$\"  width=\"195\" height=\"18\" >a) Prove that for all good functions  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/c/3ac781cb2cf4524183829aba8c612e3ff4801dd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f: \\mathbb{Q}^+ \\to \\mathbb{Q}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/6/18674a78cc8d0f471bfaf93bbcd8f7c16ce5f76e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z \\in \\mathbb{Q}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" >  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff309d483c28da3325729e58e9ff45b1f2a7e2ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"$$f(x)+f(y)+f(z) \\geq 8f(x+y+z)$$\"  width=\"278\" height=\"18\" >b) Does there exists a good functions  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/c/3ac781cb2cf4524183829aba8c612e3ff4801dd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f: \\mathbb{Q}^+ \\to \\mathbb{Q}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/6/18674a78cc8d0f471bfaf93bbcd8f7c16ce5f76e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z \\in \\mathbb{Q}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" > such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/7/61730fe07e7ae3ce923ae9444608ad41788c9c5a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"$$f(x)+f(y)+f(z) &lt; 9f(x+y+z) ?$$\"  width=\"288\" height=\"18\" >",
    "post_canonical": "We call a function $f: \\mathbb{Q}^+ \\to \\mathbb{Q}^+$ [i]good[/i] if for all $x,y \\in \\mathbb{Q}^+$ we have: $$f(x)+f(y)\\geq 4f(x+y).$$\na) Prove that for all good functions  $f: \\mathbb{Q}^+ \\to \\mathbb{Q}^+$ and $x,y,z \\in \\mathbb{Q}^+$  $$f(x)+f(y)+f(z) \\geq 8f(x+y+z)$$\nb) Does there exists a good functions  $f: \\mathbb{Q}^+ \\to \\mathbb{Q}^+$ and $x,y,z \\in \\mathbb{Q}^+$ such that $$f(x)+f(y)+f(z) < 9f(x+y+z) ?$$",
    "username": "matinyousefi",
