   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 2361976,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 418635,
    "poster_id": 67223,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\"  width=\"72\" height=\"13\" > be a convex pentagon such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/8/718f2ad40de1ddd30809fdb12fb113c44647d550.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC \\parallel AE,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"19\" > <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/e/eae9a5cde86a09c593bdb8658dce06de637f0a63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = BC +  AE,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"136\" height=\"16\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/8/ba83e22a039fbcf43af334cece31e18d0a59b59e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC = \\angle CDE.$\"  width=\"140\" height=\"13\" > Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\"  width=\"19\" height=\"12\" > be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/b/7fbe9503f0fe202abfc5d52bfbd97462c929a86b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"33\" height=\"16\" > and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"12\" > be the circumcenter of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/b/fcb9c01a2041b035894753449258b3754d538a5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD.$\"  width=\"48\" height=\"12\" > Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/0/f80d3952323a0de045dc28f5bee1465173e62fff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DMO = 90^{\\circ},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" > prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/0/9f0224d9f656d28b8fdff20961aa0a7ef96ee21d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\angle BDA = \\angle CDE.$\"  width=\"150\" height=\"13\" ><br>\n<br>\n<i>Proposed by Nazar Serdyuk, Ukraine</i>",
    "post_canonical": "Let $ABCDE$ be a convex pentagon such that $BC \\parallel AE,$ $AB = BC +  AE,$ and $\\angle ABC = \\angle CDE.$ Let $M$ be the midpoint of $CE,$ and let $O$ be the circumcenter of triangle $BCD.$ Given that $\\angle DMO = 90^{\\circ},$ prove that $2 \\angle BDA = \\angle CDE.$\n\n[i]Proposed by Nazar Serdyuk, Ukraine[/i]",
    "username": "Amir Hossein",
    "post_number": 1,
    "post_format": "bbcode",
