    "post_rendered": "Vertices and Edges of a regular <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" >-</span>gon are numbered <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/8/838228ac8ee711eda2bdae0818393f87407dbc66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,\\dots,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" > clockwise such that edge <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\"  width=\"5\" height=\"12\" > lies between vertices <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c552ffdc004c4397bbf5479ef4127de725f04117.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i,i+1 \\mod n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"115\" height=\"16\" >.</span> Now non-negative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/999733ad7b9517d8a823bcad5ef0255b6230c7ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(e_1,e_2,\\dots,e_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" > are assigned to corresponding edges and non-negative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/9/4b9e39baac85ae5e62a2744146b6d8d2714f6514.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k_1,k_2,\\dots,k_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" > are assigned to corresponding vertices such that:<br>\n<span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\"  width=\"5\" height=\"12\" >)</span> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/999733ad7b9517d8a823bcad5ef0255b6230c7ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(e_1,e_2,\\dots,e_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" > is a permutation of <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/9/4b9e39baac85ae5e62a2744146b6d8d2714f6514.png\" class